# yw103 — Agent Conventions

This repo collects authoritative economic-market analyses (Fed/IMF, Ray Dalio, KR YouTube channels, etc.) and writes structured records to Notion.

## Stack
- Python 3.10+ (`pyproject.toml`)
- LLM adapters: Anthropic Claude (default `claude-sonnet-4-6`) and OpenAI
- Pydantic v2 schema in `src/yw103/schema.py`
- Notion via `notion-client`
- Sources: `src/yw103/sources/{youtube,twitter,pdf,web,rss}.py`

## House rules
- Korean prompts and Korean-language analysis output are intentional — do not translate them to English.
- Three analysis axes are load-bearing: **자산군별 / 기간별 / 거시지표 시나리오**. Don't drop or rename them.
- RSS poller (`scripts.poll_feeds`) must remain "new items only" — never re-emit already-seen entries.
- Twitter source uses the public `cdn.syndication.twimg.com` embed endpoint; no auth.
- Don't add new third-party services (paid APIs, vector DBs, etc.) without being asked.

## Style
- Match existing file structure: extractors in `sources/`, prompts in `prompts.py`, pipeline orchestration in `pipeline.py`.
- Prefer `httpx` over `requests`.
- Keep CLI entrypoints under `scripts/` and register them in `[project.scripts]`.
- No new comments unless the *why* is non-obvious.

## What to verify before reporting "done"
- `pip install -e .` succeeds.
- Touched scripts at minimum import without error: `python -c "import scripts.<name>"`.
- If you changed schema, also update `setup_notion.py` so DB columns stay in sync.
